[04:18.16] As I was thinking back*
[04:22.16] Back to a day,
[04:22.84] Where it was mid-day,
[04:23.14] But the sky was black like midnight.
[04:23.38] Seeing a lifeless body impaled by nails
[04:25.86] Suffering at the blast of hell,
[04:27.60] Caught my attention cause it looked like a blood bath as I
[04:29.28] Looked past and saw a broken man
[04:31.58] Soaked in the white hot wrath of God and I asked why.
[04:34.74] I found some answers in His bloody face.
[04:38.66] A face I began to recognize in the background of every instance of my life, I ignored.
[04:41.04] Suddenly sense these spirits flooding, soothing my rude, rude soul.
[04:41.34] Though ruined by the world's view,
[04:41.34] He wooed me,
[04:41.34] Though crude and without a clue and screwed up out of my mind
[04:41.34] He pursued me 'til He made me holy.
[04:41.34] Whole.
